		{
			"to": "nursing/notes-on-nursing",
			"why": "Fannie Farmer's book on cooking for the sick (1904) took its epigraph from Notes on Nursing, Nightingale's line that good sick cookery will save the digestion half its work."
		},
		{
			"to": "nursing/licensure",
			"why": "The first nurse registration act, North Carolina's of 1903, examined nurses in invalid cookery; Farmer's book of 1904 opened by saying invalid cookery should be the basis of every trained nurse's education."
		},
